+# UI v2 (design/v2/HANDOVER.md §6, D6, D10, D11, D13). Behind the ?ui=v2 flag; v1 ProfileScreen
+# and AccountScreen are unchanged. 30 settings → 19, in four groups and a footer.
+# Every v2 screen is presentation only: saves go through the same App handlers as v1
+# (onSave → saveProf, onSetCustomKcal, onToggleMuteMeasurements, requestMode).
+# e2e: e2e/v2-settings.spec.js
+Feature: Settings v2 — groups, identity row, Account for everyone, no sums
+
+  Background:
+    Given the v2 UI is on
+    And I open Settings from the Today header
+
+  # ── Top screen ──────────────────────────────────────────────
+  Scenario: The top screen shows who I am, a read-only readout, then the groups
+    Then I see the identity row
+    And I see a read-only readout of my daily target, mode, weight, height, body fat and activity
+    And I see the group "You" with "Body & goal" and "Units & look"
+    And I see the group "App" with "Account & data" and "Advanced"
+    And the footer links to Privacy, Terms and Who handles my data
+    And the footer reads "Fuel Log {version} · updated {patch date}"
+
+  Scenario: Signed-in identity row
+    Given I am signed in with Google as Premium
+    Then the identity row shows my avatar, my name, "Signed in with Google", my email and PREMIUM
+    And the footer shows the date I gave health-data consent
+
+  Scenario: Signed-out identity row
+    Given I am not signed in
+    Then the identity row says I am not signed in
+    And it offers "Sign in"
+
+  # ── Body & goal ─────────────────────────────────────────────
+  Scenario: Body & goal edits save automatically and survive a reload
+    When I open "Body & goal"
+    And I change my weight, height, body fat, sex and activity
+    Then "Saved" shows briefly
+    And after a reload the new values are still there
+
+  Scenario: Changing sex says the targets were updated
+    Given my sex is already set
+    When I change it
+    Then the confirmation reads "Targets updated"
+
+  Scenario: The body fat hint is always shown
+    When I open "Body & goal"
+    Then I read "Not sure? Start with 25% for men or 30% for women."
+
+  Scenario: Goal changes go through the one guarded mode path
+    When I tap MAINTAIN under "What are you doing?"
+    Then the mode is set through requestMode with source "settings"
+    And MAINTAIN is lit
+
+  Scenario: Going back to Cut early asks once
+    Given I am on a diet break with cut load remaining
+    When I tap CUT in Body & goal
+    Then the sheet "Back to cutting already?" opens
+    And the mode is unchanged until I choose "Cut anyway"
+
+  Scenario: Daily target is Auto or my own
+    Then "Auto" is selected and shows the worked-out target
+    When I choose "Set my own" and enter 2000
+    Then my daily target is 2,000 kcal and no goal lamp is lit
+    When I choose "Auto"
+    Then the worked-out target is back
+
+  Scenario: Activity uses plain labels with step ranges
+    Then the activity choices are "Mostly sitting", "Lightly active", "Active" and "Very active"
+    And each shows its step range
+
+  Scenario: Reminders
+    Then Weigh-ins offers Daily, Few / wk, Weekly and Off, stored as the weigh-in cadence
+    And Measurements offers Weekly and Off, where Off mutes the measurement reminder
+
+  Scenario: There is no sum row
+    Then nothing on Body & goal shows "target − eaten = left" or any other sum
+
+  # ── Units & look ────────────────────────────────────────────
+  Scenario: Units are chosen in one place
+    When I open "Units & look" and choose stone and pounds
+    Then the readout shows my weight in stone and pounds
+    And my stored weight is unchanged
+
+  Scenario: Theme
+    When I choose Light
+    Then the app switches to the light theme and remembers it
+
+  # ── Account & data, for everyone ────────────────────────────
+  Scenario: Signed-out users can still reach Account & data
+    Given I am not signed in
+    When I open "Account & data"
+    Then I can Download my data
+    And I am offered "Upgrade" to Premium, which opens sign-in
+    And there is no Sign out or Delete account
+
+  Scenario: Signed-in users can sign out and delete their account
+    Given I am signed in with Google as Premium
+    When I open "Account & data"
+    Then I see my Premium status, Download my data, Sign out and Delete account
+    And deleting asks me to type DELETE, exactly as v1 Account & Privacy does
+
+  # ── Advanced ────────────────────────────────────────────────
+  Scenario: Advanced explains the target
+    When I open "Advanced"
+    Then I see lean mass, BMR, maintenance, the learned adjustment, confidence and targets for each mode
+    And I can reset the learned adjustment after one confirm
+    And the aggressive-cut status is read-only (open issue O8: no Undo)
+
+  # ── Removed (D6) ────────────────────────────────────────────
+  Scenario: Diet, allergy and dislike settings are gone
+    Then no screen in Settings offers diet type, allergies or dislikes
+    And any stored diet data is left untouched
